    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99-a4">

                <pb facs="0272" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg262"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 4 in No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Sir P. Wodehouse to the
                        Duke of Newcastle.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Government House, Cape
                            Town,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 20, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord Duke:</hi> With reference to my recent
                    despatches respecting the federal and confederate war-steamers Vanderbilt and
                    Alabama, I have the honor to forward communications received from the naval
                    commander-in-chief of this station, from which your grace will learn that acts
                    of very questionable legality have been committed by the federal steamer
                    Vanderbilt.</p>
                <p>As the crew of the captured vessel have not yet reached Cape Town, I am not in a
                    position to supply your grace with more precise information by this mail.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>P. E. WODEHOUSE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
